    "primaryWinPaths": [
      "Kodama attacks with modified creatures, generating repeated basic Forests and enough mana to overwhelm the table through ordinary trampling combat.",
      "A developed board plus Overwhelming Stampede, Triumph of the Hordes, or Craterhoof Behemoth produces a decisive lethal attack.",
      "An equipped evasive threat uses trample, protection, and combat-triggered value from swords or draw engines to maintain pressure until combat becomes lethal."
    ],
    "secondaryWinPaths": [
      "Large counter creatures such as Primordial Hydra, Managorger Hydra, and Voracious Hydra remain dangerous without Kodama.",
      "Ulvenwald Oddity, Surrak and Goreclaw, and Old One Eye provide independent team-wide trample or haste pressure.",
      "Equipment and draw engines allow the deck to rebuild into a conventional mono-green midrange board after commander removal."
    ],
    "expectedPlayPattern": "Lead with a one-mana accelerator or cheap setup permanent, then cast Kodama on turn two or three with a modified attacker ready. Use equipment, counters, and landfall proliferate to make several creatures connect, converting attacks into Forests and escalating mana. Deploy draw engines and efficient threats while holding up protection or instant interaction, then close with a scalable combat finisher once the board is safely developed.",
    "structuralNecessities": [
      "35 lands with 24 Forests preserve Kodama's repeatable basic-land engine while maintaining reliable early green mana.",
      "Nine acceleration cards support early Kodama and the deck's expensive equipment, draw engines, and finishers.",
      "The equipment and counter packages provide redundant, reusable ways to make creatures modified.",
      "Creature density supports combat, creature tutors, Beast Whisperer, Chord of Calling, and Finale of Devastation.",
      "Six interaction spells and four protection spells preserve a proactive but meaningfully interactive Bracket 4 play pattern.",
      "The three finisher package provides distinct combat closes without relying on deterministic infinite combos."
    ],
    "replaceableFlex": [
      "Cultivate",
      "Thran Power Suit",
      "Bloated Contaminator",
      "Rishkar's Expertise",
      "Ram Through"
    ]
